-AUTHOR STATIC WALKTHROUGH — NO COMPILATION OR IMPLEMENTATION EXECUTION
-
-Authority and dependency graph
-The only governing scientific/interface text is the unchanged accepted v0.4 protocol hash. The old editorial status/disposition remnants in that exact document are retained as bytes. The user-supplied genuine G0 GO and reopened correction-2 authority permit source construction only. No additional scientific choice is made in code. There is no controller, scheduler client, remote access, background worker, or automatic continuation program.
-
-The producer includes dataset.hpp -> operator.hpp -> rng.hpp -> base.hpp. Dataset I/O uses io.hpp. The analyzer additionally includes inference.hpp and analyze.hpp. The FIXOUT utility includes fixin.hpp, which uses the author core. The fixture harness is an author test program and includes only its explicitly private expectation/support headers. Sharing the author's operator with the analyzer is intentional; it is not an independent audit. The separately authored auditor must reconstruct its own implementation without these files.
-
-Frozen tiers and command boundaries
-base.hpp::tier has exactly three rows: production-r1=(code1,n42000,trace64); benchmark-r1=(code3,n1024,trace64,forced t256); fixture-r1=(code2,n16,trace16). checkpoint maps word0 & 63 to 193..256 except the compiled benchmark row. No file, environment variable or CLI parameter changes these constants.
-
-producer.cpp first parses all required arguments, checks duplicate/unknown arguments and tier/thread limits, and checks the absent/empty output path. Only after this phase does it obtain its own executable hash and enter produce(). Unknown options, overrides, duplicates, missing values and bad tiers/threads exit 2 without writing. Accepted CLI has only --tier, --out, --threads. The analyzer has exactly --tier, --data, --out and optional --timing-only. The extra FIXOUT/harness executables are local fixture interfaces, not cohort overrides.
-
-Random-address construction
-rng.hpp contains all eleven exact purpose names. A Rng derives only its selected tier's eleven keys, hashing the exact study|tier|purpose ASCII bytes without a terminator. It reads the first two digest words little-endian. New-purpose enum order does not enter the key text or counter. Counter is {block,update,entity,subindex}. Output word0 is used for 32-bit values; wide() joins word0 and word1 low-first. The old adapter's uint64 checkpoint-word extraction is deliberately not inherited: the new record uses actual word0.
-
-coordinate rejects unknown purposes, blocks outside the tier, initialization/time misuse, updates outside 1..256, entities outside 32 or 96 as applicable, bits outside 0..31, and retries outside 0..255. Focal values are requested only at the actual checkpoint by the cohort implementation; constructed PHILOX checkpoints can name their explicit fixture update as required by §16. No history step requests a focal key. No address accepts target, retrieval, arm, labels, cache, scores or thread. Survival is a value-owned callback carrying only the immutable Rng and update. A tape survives a temporary Rng safely. Injected callbacks similarly own their supplied vectors.
-
-Fresh/scout/local/donor/mutation arrays are prepared without observing labels. Local mask bit b is set exactly when LOCAL_BIT word0 &31 is zero. Focal keys are generated for all 32 slots at checkpoint. Survival draw d starts its own (d,0) counter; rejected r never advances a different draw. Both targets and all retrieval arms receive the same tape. The full fixed address array is conceptually defined by coordinate-addressable Philox; materialization of unused retries is unnecessary and cannot alter any value.
-
-BIT turnover and cache order
-operator.hpp::turnover takes a const pre-state. Candidate j=32*family+slot persists throughout. Parent/probe/scout families occupy 0..95; their mismatches are computed once. A policy probe uses cache iff policy and validity bits are set and Q does not contain that slot. Every other probe is exactly pre-genotype XOR the same fresh mask. Only eligible slots can be switched.
-
-Local family construction compares the already computed three donor mismatches. It scans families 0,1,2, replacing best only on a lower mismatch or a strictly lower key at equal mismatch. Equal key preserves the earlier lower family. The chosen donor is XORed with the supplied LM. Thirty-two local mismatches plus the prior ninety-six are exactly 128 queries, even for duplicate genotypes. There is no deduplication or score penalty.
-
-Weights are uint64(1) << (32-h), between 1 and 2^32. Each draw scans unselected j in ascending order, checks the sum bound 2^39, and multiplies x*W in a full GCC unsigned 128-bit value. Lemire uses unsigned-wrap (0-W)%W, rejects exactly low64<threshold, and takes high64 on acceptance. Retry indices 0..255 are the entire loop; a need for 256 throws RETRY_CAP. Injected-vector exhaustion before that throws DRAW_EXHAUSTED. W is nonzero, the cumulative scan uses the same ascending unselected order, and selection removes candidate identity rather than genotype.
-
-Survivor slot is draw order. Parent is j%32. Post-policy is parent pre-policy XOR the survivor-slot flip bit. A post-M slot receives pre.x[parent] and valid=1; a post-F slot stays zero-cache/invalid in the value-initialized post state. No old cache is inherited or retained. Source ancestry identifiers never enter the operator. Turnover has no floating arithmetic.
-
-Six evaluations and metadata
-operator.hpp::evaluate computes E=policy&valid before any candidates. It scans eligible slots ascending and updates focal only on a strictly lower key, so key ties go to lower slot. Empty E retains slot ff/key all-ones. All six loop iterations call turnover in full from the same const state. Q is empty / E / singleton focal according to a%3. Target is rec for a<3 and inn otherwise. Metadata [0,8) is written independently for each arm, with factual bit only on a0 for r_t=1 and a3 for r_t=0. No H=0 or e=1 copying path exists.
-
-Arm fields [8,280) include queries, retry sum, D_E, d_f, accuracy, post-policy, candidate mismatch sum, and 32 eight-byte survivor rows. D_E is ancestry in E before mutation, not post-M count. d_f counts focal ancestry, not a candidate family type. Accuracy sums 32-m against the arm's own target. Numerators are the six exact CACHE-minus-FRESH differences in canonical order. F uses FF, not AF. There is no e/H normalization and no conversion between L and F.
-
-Factual history and hashes
-Initialization is INITIAL_GENOTYPE at u0, zero caches/validity, with policy all F at even b and all M at odd b. history() draws I and R at each u=1..t-1, even when the R coin is ignored at 1/2. HALF uses the tracked T_(u-2) for copy at u>=3. It updates prev2/prev1 only after using the current target. Every history turnover uses Q=0; nothing after checkpoint is simulated.
-
-statebytes is exactly 264 bytes: x[32], cache[32], policy mask, validity mask. Hist0 hashes the 12 ASCII domain bytes, u32 block, and S0 (280 bytes total). Histnext hashes digest32,u16 update,u32 target,u32 retry sum,state264 (306 bytes). The trace starts with D0 and appends each factual Du, ending with D_(t-1). Cohort history replay recomputes the same message sequence from initialization, rather than trusting stored pre-state or digest.
-
-Record byte walkthrough (all LE, no native packed struct)
-0 BRC2; 4 version u16=2; 6 length u16=2088; 8 block u32; 12 parity start; 13 r_t; 14 t u16; 16 actual checkpoint word0; 20/24 T_(t-2)/T_(t-1); 28 innovation; 32 factual target; 36 E; 40 e; 41 H; 42 focal; 43 1-r_t; 44 focal key u64; 52 policy; 56 valid; 60 history queries; 64 checkpoint queries=768; 68 history retry sum; 72 digest32. Genotypes occupy [104,232), caches [232,360). Six 280-byte arm sections fill [360,2040). Signed numerators occupy 2040/2041 i8, 2042/2044 i16, 2046/2047 i8; 2048 total queries; 2052 zero status; 2056 raw record SHA256 of [0,2056). Total record extent=2088.
-
-Arm-relative offsets are 0 a,1 target,2 retrieval,3 factual,4 Q u32; 8 queries u16,10 retries u16,12 D_E,13 d_f,14 accuracy u16,16 post-policy u32,20 candidate mismatch sum u32,24 survivors. Each survivor is j,m,post-policy,draw retries,genotype u32. Scientific equality compares [8,280) only. Signed encoding explicitly writes the low byte/word of a converted unsigned value; decoding subtracts 2^8 or 2^16 when the sign bit is present.
-
-Chunk/trace/manifest and parallelism
-Each worker owns a distinct block vector entry obtained from an atomic work counter. Its RNG addresses do not contain worker identity. Errors are collected and joined before any data file is committed. Reversed computation order is available only through the internal fixture function, not a cohort CLI. All files are serialized after workers join, in ascending block order. Chunks are fixed 1000-block divisions with the exact tier-specific final chunk. Header has BRC2CHNK, version/index/first/count/2088/tier/reserved0 and the raw producer executable digest.
-
-Trace header is BRC2TRCE, version2, tier trace count/code and sixteen zeros. Each block has u32 b, u16 t, u16 n=t and t raw digests. Manifest order is nine header lines, chunk file lines, trace file line, total_queries, complete=1. Bookkeeping files are excluded from file lines. MANIFEST.sha256 has exactly hex, two spaces, MANIFEST.txt, LF. Query total is summed from block records, not rounded from an expected production checkpoint distribution.
-
-io.hpp creates exclusive .tmp.<final> in the destination directory, writes, fchmods, fsyncs, closes, renames and fsyncs the directory. A failure leaves evidence and cannot produce complete=1 plus a valid exact inventory. Chunks and trace precede MANIFEST.txt, which precedes MANIFEST.sha256. The bounded tiers are all below 1 GiB; the producer also checks its running file-byte budget. Results use mode0400 and cannot overwrite an existing final path. DC validation requires exact regular-file inventory, not just checking listed hashes. Scheduler/EA acceptance is intentionally outside these programs.
-
-Staged analyzer reconstruction
-A: load() checks exact manifest grammar/protocol/tier/build binding, bookkeeping checksum, every named file size/hash, no extra/tmp/subdirectory/symlink, all chunk headers, ordered complete block IDs, and trace header/entries/exact size. The manifest hash is retained even when a readable manifest fails, with NONE only for absent/unreadable manifest. A failure ends analysis with A only.
-B: every record is checked for magic/version/length and record digest; all failing blocks are collected. Failure ends analysis with B only.
-C-K: a separate guarded check collects each applicable letter for every block; one semantic failure does not suppress another. C validates metadata/ranges/invalid-cache zeros/arm fields/uniqueness and static numerator bounds. D regenerates checkpoint word, t, r_t, innovation, factual target and all 32 focal keys. E requires valid=policy and E=policy&valid. F regenerates the shared tape and every complete 280-byte arm for every block from its stored state. G independently recounts ancestry/accuracy and genotype-target mismatches from stored survivor rows, checks arm counts/retry sums, and compares all numerators to both stored and replayed values. H checks structural lineage, focal and accuracy bounds. I checks payload-only identities. J checks each query field, every arm, cohort total and fresh key-derived tier checkpoint total. K fully replays all fixed trace histories, including state, both prior targets, retry sum, every trace digest and final history digest. K is timed separately.
-L runs only after C-K all pass. It accumulates integer sums/DESC rows, computes intervals, labels, derived bounds, patterns and summary, then renders all 26 canonical lines. Any exception/fallthrough gives only L in the seven-line INVALID form. Stage-3 failures contain the ascending nonempty subset C-K, never partial sums or inferences. There is no AUDIT_REPORT pretending that this author analyzer is independent.
-
-Exact inference/rendering and interpretation
-Cohort integer sums are bounded by 42000*1024=43008000; signed64 is more than sufficient. All potentially growing fraction operations and comparisons use boost::multiprecision::cpp_int, not 128-bit cross-products. Denominators are 32*n or 1024*n. Decimal h strings are represented as exact integer-over-10^18 rationals, reused in every tier. Clipping uses [-1,1] or [-1/8,1/8]. Rat reduces by arbitrary-precision gcd, normalizes denominator sign and renders zero as 0/1. Results contain no decimals.
-
-Classification follows strict first-match >delta, <-delta, strictly inside +/-epsilon, >0, <0, fallthrough. Patterns implement every ordered pair; summaries prioritize offsetting, then any adverse material endpoint, then positive material, then all negligible, then sign-only. Derived averages/differences use the base clipped interval endpoints and strict zero exclusion. DESC rows are descriptive only and partition by parity start. The reporting helper is not called by the sealed analyzer or benchmark. Its templates preserve CACHE-minus-FRESH direction, separate L/F, describe offsetting averages as opposing effects, and include the structural cap/provenance/hashed-focal qualifications. No production interpretation is generated now.
-
-Timing-only fully analyzes, computes the exact canonical string, hashes it, consumes a digest byte to prevent dead-code removal, then clears/discards the string. stdout contains only total_ns, K_ns and PASS/FAIL; no digest, aggregate, endpoint, label, result file or scientific payload is exposed. Retaining the result string until the hash is computed is deliberate.
-
-FIXIN/FIXOUT and fixture boundary
-fixin.hpp consumes ordered fields, exact widths/list lengths, canonical decimal/integer/fraction forms, known modes/tiers, all bounds and cache invariants. It parses the whole input before evaluating a path. INJECTED CHECKPOINT requires r_t before state fields; PHILOX forbids it and derives r_t from fixture-r1/block/update. HISTORY has only uN.copy, ignores R at u1/2 in target formation, and does not repeat a checkpoint header/state/tag. Its tapes use the same typed injection fields. NUMVEC vectors are range checked before exact summation. CLASSIFIER interval injection has no claim of cohort attainability. Errors have no kind body. Every successful kind emits the specified body and END LF.
-
-COND_FORGE uses the complete checkpoint input validator and checks only C_PAYLOAD,E,F_INJECTED,G,H,I. A,B,D,J,K,L are explicitly NOT_APPLICABLE. It is never wrapped in a cohort record or given an A-L PASS. FORGE_CACHE is separately constructed from fixture block3, replays all forged arms and rehashes the data while keeping history evidence unchanged, so the expected history detection is checked by the private suite. If the prescribed block has no eligible slot, the fixture fails explicitly; no favorable frequency is assumed and no block is substituted.
-
-Limits of this walkthrough
-This is an author's source reading, not independent reconstruction, source acceptance, compiler proof, execution, sanitization GO or runtime pass. All public/private separation and later gate restrictions remain in force. Non-audit production history provenance has exactly the §14.4 limitation; conditional replay cannot establish reachable history. No empirical result, runtime, resource qualification, independent key agreement, node provenance or favorable scientific outcome has been asserted.
