-## 15. Canonical results grammar
-
-### 15.1 Lexical rules
-
-**File format.**
-
-- Printable ASCII, no CR.
-- Single spaces separate tokens; no leading or trailing spaces; no blank lines.
-- Every line ends with LF, and the file ends with `END\n`.
-
-**Values.**
-
-- `<int>`: `0`, or an optional `-` followed by a nonzero digit and further digits. `-0` and `+` are forbidden.
-- `<frac>`: `<int>/<pos>`, where `<pos>` is a positive integer without leading zeros, and gcd(|p|, q) = 1. Zero is `0/1`; an integer v is `v/1`.
-- `<hex64>`: 64 lowercase hex characters.
-- `<tier>`: `production-r1`, `benchmark-r1` or `fixture-r1`. This is the tier the program was invoked with.
-- `<X>` is in the canonical endpoint order `L_rec, L_inn, P_rec, P_inn, F_rec, F_inn`.
-- `<Q>` is in the order `L, P, F`.
-- Lists are comma-separated, without spaces, in canonical order.
-
-### 15.2 VALID form (exactly 26 lines)
-
-```
-BRC2-RESULTS-V3
-status=VALID
-tier=<tier>
-manifest_sha256=<hex64>
-blocks=<n>
-ENDPOINT L_rec sum=<int> den=<32n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-ENDPOINT L_inn sum=<int> den=<32n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-ENDPOINT P_rec sum=<int> den=<1024n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-ENDPOINT P_inn sum=<int> den=<1024n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-ENDPOINT F_rec sum=<int> den=<32n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-ENDPOINT F_inn sum=<int> den=<32n> mean=<frac> lo=<frac> hi=<frac> label=<LABEL>
-DERIVED L avg_lo=<frac> avg_hi=<frac> diff_lo=<frac> diff_hi=<frac> resolved_difference=<0|1>
-PATTERN L <PATTERN>
-DERIVED P avg_lo=<frac> avg_hi=<frac> diff_lo=<frac> diff_hi=<frac> resolved_difference=<0|1>
-PATTERN P <PATTERN>
-DERIVED F avg_lo=<frac> avg_hi=<frac> diff_lo=<frac> diff_hi=<frac> resolved_difference=<0|1>
-PATTERN F <PATTERN>
-SUMMARY <SUMMARY_BODY>
-DESC H_count ALL_F=<int> ALL_M=<int>
-DESC E_hist ALL_F=<33 ints, e=0..32>
-DESC E_hist ALL_M=<33 ints, e=0..32>
-DESC R1_count ALL_F=<int> ALL_M=<int>
-DESC startsum ALL_F L_rec=<int> L_inn=<int> P_rec=<int> P_inn=<int> F_rec=<int> F_inn=<int>
-DESC startsum ALL_M L_rec=<int> L_inn=<int> P_rec=<int> P_inn=<int> F_rec=<int> F_inn=<int>
-DESC factual_A_sum ALL_F=<int> ALL_M=<int>
-END
-```
-
-**Field definitions.**
-
-- `manifest_sha256` is the SHA-256 of the `MANIFEST.txt` bytes.
-- `sum` is Σ numerator.
-- `mean`, `lo` and `hi` are the exact §8.2 values; `<LABEL>` is a §9.3 literal.
-- `<PATTERN>` is one of the 12 §9.4 literals.
-
-**`<SUMMARY_BODY>`** is exactly one of:
-
-- `S1_MATERIAL_TARGET_OFFSETTING quantities=<list of Q>`;
-- `S2_MATERIAL_ADVERSE_PRESENT endpoints=<list of X labelled MATERIAL_NEGATIVE>`;
-- `S3_MATERIAL_POSITIVE_ONLY endpoints=<list of X labelled MATERIAL_POSITIVE>`;
-- `S4_ALL_NEGLIGIBLE_WITHIN_MARGIN`;
-- `S5_NONMATERIAL_SIGN_RESOLVED endpoints=<list of X with a sign-only label>`.
-
-**DESC definitions** (counted per start):
-
-- `H_count`: blocks with H = 1.
-- `E_hist`: block counts by e.
-- `R1_count`: blocks with R_t = 1.
-- `startsum`: Σ of each numerator.
-- `factual_A_sum`: Σ A(factual arm).
-
-The DESC rows are descriptive only.
-
-**Non-production tiers** use the same grammar with their n and the same h constants. They are engineering artifacts, compared by hash only and never read or summarized.
-
-### 15.3 INVALID form (exactly 7 lines)
-
-```
-BRC2-RESULTS-V3
-status=INVALID
-tier=<tier>
-manifest_sha256=<hex64|NONE>
-failed_checks=<comma list of letters A..L, ascending>
-SUMMARY S0_INVALID
-END
-```
-
-**Field rules.**
-
-- `manifest_sha256` is `NONE` iff `MANIFEST.txt` is absent or unreadable.
-- `failed_checks` follows the §14.3 staging exactly:
-  - `A`;
-  - or `B`;
-  - or the nonempty subset of C–K that failed;
-  - or `L`.
-
-The INVALID form contains no sums, means, intervals, labels or patterns. None is fabricated.
-
-### 15.4 Classifier and arithmetic tests
-
-- **Attainable-cohort arithmetic** is tested with NUMVEC fixtures (§16.1). These are numerator vectors that respect every static range.
-- **Boundary cases** are tested by direct injection of rational intervals (CLASSIFIER fixtures), never as claimed 42,000-block vectors. Boundary cases are exact equality at δ or ε, and the fallthrough.
-
